Orin Stage uses the Ubuntu distribution Python, but bundles an exact private
Python application closure under /usr/lib/orin-stage/venv.  This preserves one
application dependency contract across Jammy and Noble while keeping CPython,
the compiler toolchain, and system libraries distro-provided.

All Python sdists and the Cargo vendor tree are verified source inputs in the
separate deps orig component.  The package build is intentionally offline once
Build-Depends have been installed from Ubuntu.

This is a PPA-oriented MVP packaging model, not a claim of Debian archive
upstream-policy suitability.

The tracked `debian/changelog` uses an unsuffixed, `UNRELEASED` version as the
canonical packaging revision.  `prepare_debian_source.py` localizes only the
changelog copied into the generated source tree.  For the 0.2.1 release, these
commands produce the target PPA versions:

```
python3 tools/release/prepare_debian_source.py \
  --series jammy \
  --ppa-revision 1 \
  --output release/dependencies/generated/debian-source-jammy

python3 tools/release/prepare_debian_source.py \
  --series noble \
  --ppa-revision 1 \
  --output release/dependencies/generated/debian-source-noble
```

The generated changelog versions are `0.2.1-1~jammy1` and
`0.2.1-1~noble1`, with matching `jammy` and `noble` distributions.  The
upstream orig version remains 0.2.1.  The helper does not sign, upload, tag, or
create a GitHub release.
